# What the image build is allowed to see.
#
# The Dockerfile copies three things -- pyproject.toml, README.md and src/ --
# so everything is excluded first and those are named back in. A denylist would
# have to grow every time the working tree does; this way a new virtualenv, a
# saved capture or somebody's scratch notes can never quietly enlarge the
# context. The cost is that a new COPY needs a matching line here.
#
# Without this file the context is ~414 MB, almost all of it .venv and
# .mypy_cache; with it, about a megabyte.

*

!pyproject.toml
!README.md
!src

# Artefacts that live inside the tree just re-included above.
src/**/__pycache__
src/**/*.py[cod]
src/**/*.egg-info
